      "body": "Tracking issue: #37742. Related: #40702 (exposes `think_mode` through the image API).\r\n\r\n## Motivation\r\n\r\nWith `think_mode=True`, `t2i_generate` decodes the reasoning, `</think>` and `<img>` into the\r\ncondition KV cache, and starts the image RoPE t-index after them. But it still passes the\r\npre-think prompt length as `prefix_lengths` to `prepare_flash_kv_cache`. That sets\r\n`actual_seq_lengths_kv = prompt_len + image_len`, and `_flash_or_sdpa` compacts K/V to\r\n`k[:, :prompt_len] ++ k[:, prefix_width:]` in every layer at every denoising step. So the image\r\ntokens never see the reasoning, `</think>` or `<img>`, while their positions assume they follow\r\nthem, and every think-mode image is noise. This affects the CUDA, CPU and NPU-FIA paths; it came\r\nin with the batched-generation change (#39382), which introduced `prefix_lengths`.\r\n\r\n## Modification\r\n\r\nAfter the think decode, `condition_prefix_lengths` becomes the cache length (`t_index + 1`,\r\nthe same value the image t-index starts at). Think mode only accepts one prompt, so there is\r\nno padding to account for.\r\n\r\n## Tests\r\n\r\n- `test_sensenova_u1_think_mode_image_attends_to_reasoning`: a tiny random NEO-Unify model on\r\n  CPU, 4 think tokens; the think-mode image must match the one computed with the whole prefix\r\n  visible (`prefix_lengths=None`, valid for one unpadded prompt). Fails on main\r\n  (3043 / 3072 elements differ), passes with the fix.\r\n- GPU, 1x H200, SenseNova-U1.5-8B-MoT, CFG 4, seed 42, `think_mode=True`. On the real model,\r\n  the cache length after the think decode equals `t_index + 1` in every run, and the\r\n  reasoning text is byte-identical before and after the fix; only the denoise attention changes.\r\n  - 2048x2048, 50 steps, default think budget (1024): two prompts (a bakery price poster; a\r\n    clock at a quarter past three next to a calendar on the winter-solstice month). On main\r\n    both images are structureless noise. With the fix both are coherent: a \"SUNRISE BAKERY\"\r\n    poster with three priced items, and a wall clock beside a \"DECEMBER 21ST\" desk calendar\r\n    (the reasoning resolved the solstice date; the clock hands and the item names are not\r\n    accurate). Wall time is unchanged (32.3 / 27.9 s on main vs 33.2 / 28.1 s, mostly the\r\n    think decode).\r\n\r\n<img width=\"1060\" height=\"1100\" alt=\"think_main_vs_fix\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6e313d99-5b7f-4e34-b4b1-b07c01b383ae\" />\r\n\r\n  - The setting from 40702 (1024x1024, 10 steps, 64-token think budget), three prompts\r\n    including 40702's \"A clean technology poster with structured layout and clear\r\n    typography.\": main, and 40702's head (2164d5903a), give noise. Their PNGs are\r\n    byte-identical even though 40702 changes which think tokens are cached, because none of\r\n    them reach the image. The commit before #39382 and this fix both give coherent images. A\r\n    64-token or ~220-330-token reasoning, and 2048x2048 / 50 steps, behave the same way.\r\n\r\n<img width=\"1200\" height=\"948\" alt=\"think_1024_main_pr40702_pre39382_fix\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f1128574-e7bf-4de0-9474-8273f9192348\" />\r\n\r\n\r\n- Non-think requests never reach the changed branch.\r\n\r\n## Notes\r\n\r\n- Output changes for every `think_mode=True` request; non-think requests are untouched.\r\n- #40702 exposes `think_mode` through the API; without this fix those requests return noise.\r\n- Conflicts textually with the SenseNova CFG-parallel change, which moves this code into\r\n  `_t2i_think_prefill`; whichever lands second carries the one-line change over.\r\n- Not fixed here: on Ascend without FIA, a think request with `batch_size > 1` builds its\r\n  dense mask from the pre-think `key_valid_mask`, which is shorter than the cache. Not run on NPU.\r\n\r\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\r\n\r\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\r\n---\r\n### CI States\r\n\r\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #39248421889](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39248421889)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\r\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39248421810](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39248421810)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\r\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #39248421839](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39248421839)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\r\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
